999
M7.3 release fixture (M7 spec 22, Fixture C): a circle carrying a RADIAL
999
dimension, and a second circle carrying a DIAMETRIC one.
999

999
Circle 1: centre (25, 30), drawn radius 9.8, dimensioned radius 10.
999
Circle 2: centre (80, 30), drawn radius 14.7, dimensioned diameter 30.
999

999
Both are drawn 2% under their dimensioned size -- inside the agreement band,
999
so association still resolves and the SOLVER is what corrects them. A curve
999
dimension is matched on CENTRE and cross-checked on SIZE, so unlike the
999
rectangle fixture the drawn size cannot be wildly wrong: that would be a
999
drawing contradicting itself, which reconstruction refuses on purpose.
999

999
The two dimensions carry DIFFERENT kinds on purpose. Radial states the centre
999
outright (code 10) and a rim point (code 15); DIAMETRIC states two OPPOSITE
999
rim points and never states the centre at all. A reader that treated the two
999
alike would place the diametric centre a full radius out, where it matches no
999
circle -- so this file fails loudly if that is ever done.
999

999
Analytical oracle after reconstruction, extruded 30 mm:
999
  circle 1 alone: pi x 10^2 x 30
999
and doubling its Radius parameter to 20 must give exactly 4x that.
